  "review_fixes": [
    "Stale entry status \"installed\" after hub_remove when snapshots are chained (found by Qt bridge validation); statuses now recomputed each refresh, regression tests fail without the fix.",
    "Reinstall of the retained previous version returns version_retained_use_rollback instead of colliding.",
    "Namespace unlink is skipped unless the namespace dir is still private (never through a replaced symlink)."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Install means promote to private namespace only; no extraction, loader or runtime until S3.",
    "Qt install click is not driven end to end: lifecycle UI phase observes a CLI-driven install and drives remove (confirm/cancel) through the real UI.",
    "Quarantined plugins are only removable; orphan files in hub-plugins are never auto-deleted.",
    "Source of payload still only via offline CLI scripts/hub_import.py.",
    "with_approvals still rehashes staged and installed payloads synchronously per refresh.",
    "Publisher unauthenticated; no Base command authority granted.",
    "Physical audio, CPAL/PipeWire/AEC/hotplug/barge-in, real Wayland and relocatable packaging require implementation; no personal devices used."
  ],
